Frank Mittelbach forwarded me two changes in a task description to move the
current version of the master task list to 3.0a.  The changes are:

1.  The status of the "Bibliography style programming" task has been moved
to pending because of the in-development status of BibTeX1.

2.  A new task has been added following "Bibliography style programming"
and prior to "Timing tests":
+ \task{Bibliography style requirements}
+
+ Collect available \BibTeX.99 styles and if possible further journal
+ and publisher requirements regarding bibiographies and analyze them.
+ Summarize the functionality of each style, whether or not it is easily
+ programmable with the current \BibTeX{}, what special functions would
+ be helpful, etc.
+
+ \timeestimate{1-3 weeks for collecting information}
+
+ \timeestimate{1-3 hours for each style}
+
+ \coordinator{18 September 1992}{Robert Tolksdorf}\email{tolk@cs.tu-berlin.de}
+ \othervolunteers
+ %\volunteer{NAME}\email{}

Please note that I have taken the liberty of tentatively moving Robert
Tolksdorf, formerly coordinator of "Bibliography style programming", to the
coordinator of this task as it was in concert with his interests.

As usual, the updated master task list file is available for anonymous ftp
retrieval from:
 [VMS] Niord.SHSU.edu:[FILESERV.VOL-TASK]VOL-TASK.TEX
